    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/84-drill-reach (56dfa8e), gating now:\n- new `operation/drill_reach.rs`: every drilling cycle (axial and cross) refuses by name a hole deeper from the stock surface than the tool's flute (`flute_len`) - e.g. \"cross hole 0 ... is 16.000 mm deep from the stock surface; tool DR-0400's flute reaches 12.000 mm\"; the holder (`holder_d` x `holder_len`, at `flute_len + shank_len` behind the tip) must stay above the material on axial holes and above the stock top or outside the stock radius on every cross-drill move - the end-face swing is refused (raise Clearance to drill it).\n- 7 existing fixtures were real reach collisions (e.g. a 31 mm through hole on a 12 mm flute) - their test drills now have flutes long enough; the old \"deep hole warns but still generates\" test is now a refusal test.\n- tests: drill_reach (4, three failed on main) + 2 unit tests.\n- known cost: a hole on a pocket floor with stock declared may be falsely refused (drilling doesn't know what earlier ops removed) - filed as #89.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
