    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T16:11:32Z",
    "body": "claimed: main session (review fixes for PR #90) · 2026-11-07T16:11Z · branch issue/84-drill-reach · plan: the independent review found no blocker but: (1) Bore/BackBore/Tap held to the flute although they run in an existing hole - false refusal (check shank vs hole diameter + holder instead); (2) the cross holder check uses one global stock radius/top - a stepped shaft is refused by a far-away flange (measure per Z band); (3) fail-open: a shank wider than the drill sits up to ~1 mm inside stock at an off-centre cross mouth (use max(d, shank_d)); (4) fail-open: a NaN holder_d/holder_len reads as no holder (refuse by name). Box corner-radius depth -> #85 (raised to P1); counterbore / faced-stock depth -> #89.",
